Third-party software in bt-headset-hid
======================================

bt-headset-hid itself is licensed under the MIT License, see the file LICENSE.

The program bt-headset-hid (/usr/bin/bt-headset-hid in the packages) is a
statically linked Go program. Besides bt-headset-hid's own code it contains
the third-party code listed below. Their licenses allow distributing it in
binary form together with MIT-licensed code, on the condition that their
copyright notices, conditions and disclaimers accompany every copy; this file
does that. The packages install it next to LICENSE.

The program is built without cgo, so it contains no C library (no glibc). The
packages and archives contain no third-party icons, images, fonts or sounds:
the tray icon uses icon names from the desktop's own icon theme.

`go version -m /usr/bin/bt-headset-hid` lists the Go version and the modules
built into the program; packaging/check-licenses.sh checks this file against
that list when the packages are built.

Contents

  1. github.com/godbus/dbus/v5 v5.2.4      BSD-2-Clause
  2. The Go standard library and runtime   BSD-3-Clause, with the Go patent
     (including golang.org/x/net etc.      grant; some files also carry the
     vendored into it)                     notices in 2a to 2c

Not included in the program: golang.org/x/sys, listed in go.mod, is only
used by godbus on FreeBSD and is not built into the Linux program. contrib/pipewire-1.0-fix.sh downloads PipeWire's sources (MIT) from
PipeWire's site and builds them on the user's own computer; the packages
contain no PipeWire code.

